{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world","id":1089029,"title":"We ever going to get a World of Dreams, OR Dream Across the World?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T00:18:45-07:00","id":1089029,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> We ever going to get a World of Dreams, OR Dream Across the World?","content":"So I really dig the expansion of the basic Kithain to 13! And I always loved the quality of the Nunnehi, and Hsien, and I need to read the Menehune.<br /> <br /> So are we ever going to get a big book expanding on the Kingdoms across the World? It would be a great place to add in at least the basics of Gallain core groups. The most needed in my opinion are the Changeling Kiths of the Land of Ancient Tales (Africa), Land of the Wandering Dream (Australia and New Zealand, I hella really want Aboriginal Australian Changelings and really any World of Darkness Australia material!), India, Central and South America!<br /> <br /> And maybe a handful of others, like Leshii and Domovoi mentioned in Empire of the Firebird, maybe mention of a Djinn group, like Ifrit, Murid, Gul, ect. And other Misc like Oni, Hellhounds, Imps (well mainly because I made them kiths in my canon :P).<br /> <br /> But really I woud be antsy to expand Africa to more then Eshu/Oba like Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom did with Laibon. And I feel India and Australia would have such big mythic ties that I abhor the vacuum of the current state, yeah I mean what so far we only have Naraka and Hanumen?<br /> <br /> But man back when I first discovered changeling with back copies of 2nd ed I really was fascinated by the Kingdoms only briefly mentioned!<br /> <br /> Are we going to get such a book?<br /> <br /> What Changeling Books do you most want? And what Kiths/ Group of associated Gallain do you most think we need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:06:19-07:00","id":1089124,"title":"","content":"I would <i>love</i> a Kithbook: Ghille Dhu.<br /> <br /> A sourcebook on African changelings would be awesome too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:37:52-07:00","id":1089142,"title":"","content":"It seems like a lot of people were disappointed by the mostly cursory and stereotypical handling the non-American parts of the globe got, so a Dreams Across the World book seems like something people would be interested in.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see a book that gives full details on the Gallain. They were super-compressed to fit in C20 and didn't have space to fix most of the problems they had previously (namely, that most of them are just <i>there</i> and don't fit into the game in any obvious way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:51:54-07:00","id":1089151,"title":"","content":"I'd like a book about the Land of Ancient Tales where the locals changelings aren't just presented as offshoots of northern changelings like the La\u00efbon were in Vampire.<br /> I 'd like books about the Kiths of India, Iran, South East Asia, South America (especially Brazil since Umbanda and Quimbanda actually have Eshus spirits) and Europe beyond the British islands.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:06:18-07:00","id":1089160,"title":"","content":"I'd like a World of Dreams, a book on Changeling politics across the world, an alternate eras sourcebook, a Book of Nightmares, the Codex Compendia, a Dreaming sourcebook like &quot;Umbra&quot; or &quot;Infinite Tapestry&quot;. <br /> <br /> Seriously, I could go on all day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:43:43-07:00","id":1089219,"title":"","content":"I'd like a dual DA:F C20 setting sourcebook, divided in half, focused on the Shattering: one half is just <i>before</i> the Shattering, while the other half is the chaos immediately <i>following</i> the Shattering. It could have conversion rules, as players may well like the idea of their Firstborn smith being trapped on Earth, transforming into a boggan or a nocker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:58:31-07:00","id":1089326,"title":"","content":"Yes, a look at fae across the world and a more developed and nuanced portrayal of non-North American kingdoms would be my number one Wanted Thing for the game line. I'd back a KS for it in a heartbeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13035-snumpus","name":"Snumpus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:13:13-07:00","id":1089370,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see the Changeling universe expanded.<br /> <br /> But... I still lament the loss of the stuff made by Spikey on the Shadownessence forums. He had made both Djinn and Asura kiths, and they really worked wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:53:46-07:00","id":1089398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world?p=1089219#post1089219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a dual DA:F C20 setting sourcebook, divided in half, focused on the Shattering: one half is just <i>before</i> the Shattering, while the other half is the chaos immediately <i>following</i> the Shattering. It could have conversion rules, as players may well like the idea of their Firstborn smith being trapped on Earth, transforming into a boggan or a nocker.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit that some of my early drafts of the history section was a lot like you describe. In the end, however, Changeling has to be the dominant factor in this case, but as you can see in the PDF, there's a lot of Fae in there.<br /> <br /> Don't know how many times I pestered Maggie and Charlie with new versions throughout the first draft process. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:03:01-07:00","id":1089408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rigistrade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world?p=1089398#post1089398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to admit that some of my early drafts of the history section was a lot like you describe. In the end, however, Changeling has to be the dominant factor in this case, but as you can see in the PDF, there's a lot of Fae in there.<br /> <br /> Don't know how many times I pestered Maggie and Charlie with new versions throughout the first draft process. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It means a lot, and creativity should be king for a game like Changeling: The Dreaming or Dark Ages: Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:26:49-07:00","id":1089638,"title":"","content":"So is there really anything stopping Kithain from being born into things like Native American bodies? We know the Nunnehi had a different ritual to survive the Shattering and bound themselves into the Bloodlines of the American Peoples, so do you think that interferes and perhaps a stakes a claim so Kithain aren't randomly born into them? I get the Feeling the Kithain have to spread into regions before they are born into new peoples. So they performed the changeling way Ritual and were born into the first Generation close to their Ancestral Homes, and at first were born into bloodlines, but after forming into shared courts and interbreeding we have had examples of two changelings of different Kiths having a child be a third kith. Are all Changelings in some way physically related to other changelings by blood, or once changelings start breeding into a culture they sort of have reincarnation by osmosis to even unrelated families while strongly favoring people with Fae Ancestry? So once changelings start breeding with Aboriginal peoples you will get things like a Pookah of Coyote in the Plains tribes without being related to a Kithain?<br /> <br /> I want to wonder how hard it is for Pooka to smuggle into tribal cultures outside of Europe, so Pookah born in an Area dominated by Nunnehi, or Hsien, or beyond the courts of the Oba?<br /> <br /> Or could a group of Pookah be adopted into the Nunnehi's ritual of reincarnating their way through their chosen families?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I would be interested in more Noble Houses. Hear me out, I think it is fine if the Noble houses we have are all of the Sidhe ones, but for instance the Merfolk introduced the concept of non Sidhe Noble houses! So I think places like say the Empire of the Firebird, India and Mexico would be great places to introduce Newly Discovered Noble Houses of Other Cultures. Like a House of the Smoking Mirror, House Veles, and House Zmeivitch for Unseelie, and House of the Feathered Serpent, and House Bogtyr for the Seelie.<br /> <br /> I would love things like Arts of the Sun and Moon in say a Russia section. And would we be able to have native Kithain style Gallain in the Land of Eight Million Dreams, or would making an Oni be a Hsien, even though they don't really fit their Elemental Noble, animal Commoner divide, well I guess you could go with the Ox and Horse for Gozu/Niutou and Mezu/Mamien. But would the Dreaming be like virgin territory since the local &quot;Changelings&quot; are not aspected to Dreams but to the Spirits?<br /> <br /> <br /> And I would love more Hsien Arts, their Magics are really cool and we get a lot of stuff in a simple 5 elements and 1 Internal Alchemy Design, but I would like more! MOAAAR! What would they be? Perhaps an art tied to Auspiciousness itself? One tied to the Sun and Moon would fit here too. I would like more Indian themed Hsien!<br /> <br /> Actually it really feels like India is the middle point of all the World of Darkness, it really is always were the East and West meet, the dividing line. So maybe India has a native family of Gallain Kiths and Hsien?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:39:05-07:00","id":1089641,"title":"","content":"Ohhh Also wouldn't Inanimae be popping up in the Territory of the Hsien and Nunnehi? They aren't specifically tied to Europeans right, they are Universal? After all the Woody dudes are Kuberas and that is pretty Eastern with your Vedic goodness yum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:37:38-07:00","id":1089722,"title":"","content":"Of course Inanimae are in Asia. They're born of the <i>planet's</i> dreams, thus being utterly independent of a 'human genesis'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:13:30-07:00","id":1090216,"title":"","content":"Just curious Rage Across Appalachia is a Werewolf Changeling Crossover book, and my current game is a Wyld West Werewolf game that will deal with Changelings, so is the book any good? Cassada if I recall was always a pretty good writer.<br /> <br /> I thought this book was compiled into one of those double books, and I bought the one I was missing Rage Across the World Vol. 2 but it was Australia and Vancouver, glad I got the Australia portion though wanted that one for a while. But wasn't it in a double book? I seem to recall Valkenburg and I think Monkeywrench were another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:17:00-07:00","id":1090220,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a look at the Middle East/Persia drawing on 1001 Nights, and tying in connections between &quot;djinn&quot; and &quot;fae&quot;, with new kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:42:22-07:00","id":1090231,"title":"","content":"A new Blood-dimmed Tides would also be nice, especially if it brought the merfolk out of their isolation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T05:09:53-07:00","id":1090245,"title":"","content":"Book of Freeholds may be getting afew new kiths and out of Concordia writeups.. as for more Hsien powers, Hsien powers seem very much like Mage powers its hard to &quot;add&quot; without it getting weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:20:07-07:00","id":1090260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world?p=1090245#post1090245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of Freeholds may be getting afew new kiths</div> </div> </div> </div>We packed a crazy amount of stuff into a small amount of word count. The sleep deprivation that comes with having a small baby could be making me misremember, but even with all that, I don't think we added any new kiths in that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":".  Clarity 05-09-2017, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T11:32:50-07:00","id":1090388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world?p=1090260#post1090260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We packed a crazy amount of stuff into a small amount of word count. The sleep deprivation that comes with having a small baby could be making me misremember, but even with all that, I don't think we added any new kiths in that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>AH well you talked about putting some of the Wyld Hunt Kiths in a book and that's the only one out there...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:00:25-07:00","id":1090406,"title":"","content":"Oooooh! No, I talked about doing some fan write-ups of them to post on the forum, one of which is here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1048706-arcadia-ccg-kiths#post1048706\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...hs#post1048706</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T13:44:35-07:00","id":1090463,"title":"","content":"I would love to see this if it was written by people of the realavent cultures. Too much of Changeling has been the dreams white Americans have of the rest of the world, and the exceptions have generally been authors who aren't white Americans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T09:28:19-07:00","id":1094588,"title":"","content":"Some time ago I've written about Spain and Chile with some new Kiths (in spanish):<br /> <br /> Ensue\u00f1o en Espa\u00f1a: La Tierra de las Estaciones (Dreaming in Spain: The Land of Seasons)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.bibliotecadecartago.net/pafiledb.php?action=file&amp;id=664\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.bibliotecadecartago.net/p...on=file&amp;id=664</a><br /> <br /> Ensue\u00f1o en Chile: La Tierra de las Dos Serpientes (Dreaming in Chile: The Land of the Two Snakes)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://webvampiro.mforos.com/542820/12865981-ensueno-en-chile-la-tierra-de-las-dos-serpientes/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://miarroba.st/224/logos/normal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://webvampiro.mforos.com/542820/12865981-ensueno-en-chile-la-tierra-de-las-dos-serpientes/\" target=\"_blank\"> Ensue&ntilde;o en Chile: la Tierra de las Dos Serpientes </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://webvampiro.mforos.com/542820/12865981-ensueno-en-chile-la-tierra-de-las-dos-serpientes/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://webvampiro.mforos.com/542820/12865981-ensueno-en-chile-la-tierra-de-las-dos-serpientes/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Las serpientes Treng Treng y Cai Cai. Ilustraci&amp;oacute;n de Edward Bohle Bueno, pues tras la publicaci&amp;oacute;n de Necr&amp;oacute;polis: Chile, este a&amp;ntilde;o le toca a la parte del Ensue&amp;ntilde;o, con duendes y hadas chilenos. Cualquier idea, sugerencia o aportaci&amp;oacute;n, ser&amp;aacute; bien recibida. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T12:27:53-07:00","id":1094916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world?p=1090220#post1090220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see a look at the Middle East/Persia drawing on 1001 Nights, and tying in connections between &quot;djinn&quot; and &quot;fae&quot;, with new kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is my wet dream.<br /> <br /> I don't really look forward to anything related to South America/Africa because they tend to be infested with dumb stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T12:42:33-07:00","id":1094918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sinister Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world?p=1094916#post1094916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is my wet dream.<br /> <br /> I don't really look forward to anything related to South America/Africa because they tend to be infested with dumb stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a matter of getting the right writer. I would be very interested if Onyx Path could perhaps recruit Jerry D Grayson to work on some Africa-related material (he's doing &quot;Ifri&quot; [not-Africa] for 7th Sea 2nd Edition currently).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T12:58:31-07:00","id":1094922,"title":"","content":"That would be good, but I don't hold my hopes up. Bellatierra's entry basically says 'Nobody gives a crap about South America. We think there is a jungle kingdom and a mountain kingdom.' Same goes for Africa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T17:41:37-07:00","id":1094976,"title":"","content":"A changeling city book, the way Mage got that Las Vegas book &quot;Fallen Towers,&quot; would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:56:17-07:00","id":1095228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world?p=1089370#post1089370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see the Changeling universe expanded.<br /> <br /> But... I still lament the loss of the stuff made by Spikey on the Shadownessence forums. He had made both Djinn and Asura kiths, and they really worked wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm always torn on this issue. Namely because so many people have written so much for these lands, it would almost be heartbreaking to see all their hard work, research, and passionate writing be overruled. I know it would probably never happen, but I would love it if people could submit their home-written stuff for consideration. <br /> <br /> Impractical, I know, but it would be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T02:15:23-07:00","id":1105317,"title":"","content":"For C20 I would most love a large Dream Across the World book Detailing the World through the Eyes of Changelings, and including things not really covered like Australia, Under the Sea, Under the Earth, Africa, India and the Rest of Asia.<br /> <br /> I would also like the Books of Glamour we were going to get ages ago, have it include rules for Treasures, and assortment of Treasures, and more info on Glades/Freeholds and other things. Maybe include arts and glamour and enchantment here.<br /> <br /> A large kith Book fleshing out all the Kiths in one book.<br /> <br /> A large Gallain Book with a section for Menehune, Hsien, Nunnehi (Including South American and Central American Nunnehi as they mentioned they belong to this group as well), Merfolk, and African Fae, Australian Fae and Inanimae and Adhene. Hell I would love a book for each of these things, but in the meantime one for all of them would be nice, or possibly one for Inanimae, One for Hsien, One for Nunnehi/Menehune/Merfolk, and One for the new gallain types yet to be fleshed out like from Australia. And an Adhene Book.<br /> <br /> A C20 Shadow Court book, with most of the Emphasis on Thallain, at least half the book, and an appendix on Autumn Folk.<br /> <br /> One big book on Houses, and toss in some houses from other cultures mentioned/splatted perhaps first in a Dream Across the World Book.<br /> <br /> This would make me hella happy. With an Extra book for Australia, one for India.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T15:29:27-07:00","id":1107139,"title":"","content":"I don't think getting an official rulebook will in any way invalidate fan-made material.<br /> Changeling fans are already used to houseruling stuff in or out anyways. (See the Hsien thread if you don't believe me)<br /> It's the Dreaming's way<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T10:50:51-07:00","id":1110258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world?p=1090245#post1090245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of Freeholds may be getting afew new kiths and out of Concordia writeups.. as for more Hsien powers, Hsien powers seem very much like Mage powers its hard to &quot;add&quot; without it getting weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, we didn't really have any space for new kiths, but one of my goals as the dev for the book was to include writeups for freeholds in all parts of the world. While most of the 40+ freeholds talked about within the pages are only short blurbs, there are nine or ten fully statted examples of Glades and freeholds for player use and ... *counts* maybe two or three of them are in North America? The rest (and a significant chunk of the smaller blurbs) are scattered across the world with what my writers strove for respect in their real-world locations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T11:34:41-07:00","id":1110279,"title":"","content":"Well, there are a lot of different types of Changelings. The Hsien seem to be refugees from the High Umbra that have nothing to do with the Dreaming, though that is debatable. The Kinain are refugees from the Dreaming that have nothing to do with the Umbra. The Nunnehi are refugees from the Dreaming that survived the Shattering by bonding with Middle Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:25:44-07:00","id":1111036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089029-we-ever-going-to-get-a-world-of-dreams-or-dream-across-the-world?p=1110279#post1110279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there are a lot of different types of Changelings. The Hsien seem to be refugees from the High Umbra that have nothing to do with the Dreaming, though that is debatable. The Kinain are refugees from the Dreaming that have nothing to do with the Umbra. The Nunnehi are refugees from the Dreaming that survived the Shattering by bonding with Middle Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that the Nunnehi have always had a foot in both the Dreaming and the Umbra, because for them the two are not all that separate. The spirit realm is essentially the realm of concepts that exist in the Autumn world. Meanwhile the Dreaming is the realm of concepts that have yet to be. One is possibility, the other the shadows of what are. The Nunnehi are a bit of both, and anot expanded exploration of how they overlap would be a fantastic edition to the lore I think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T19:23:12-07:00","id":1114862,"title":"","content":"I would love to have more details of fae around the world. However, it would need to be integrated with Changeling, better than the Hsien are. Of all of the WoD games, the expansion of Changeling into other parts of the world has created the biggest mess. It seems like every time a new area is brought up it comes with an entirely new set of game mechanics, which is frustrating to me. The Nunnehi are an example of how to do it right, as they are instantly recognizable as &quot;changelings&quot;, use the same basic system, but have some slight differences that are more tweaks rather than a completely new design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}